        "contact": {
          "name": "Dymo API Support",
          "url": "https://tpe.li/D-DMAPI"
        },
        "description": "The Dymo API provides a comprehensive solution for businesses by integrating security, AI, marketing, and analytics into a single platform. It allows users to validate data, detect malicious activity, and enhance marketing strategies while gaining insights into customer behavior.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production server",
            "url": "https://api.dymo.com/v1"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Dymo API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "All-in-one validation and fraud-detection API covering email, phone, IP, IBAN, crypto wallet, URL and credit card data",
        "homepage": "https://dymo.tpeoficial.com/products/dymo-api",
        "docs_url": "https://docs.tpeoficial.com/docs/dymo-api/getting-started/introduction",
        "about_md": "Dymo API is a data-validation and security gateway built by [TPEOficial](https://dymo.tpeoficial.com/). It bundles several checks normally spread across separate services into a single HTTP API aimed at signup flows, CRMs and marketing platforms that need to keep junk and malicious users out.\n\nWhat you can do with the API:\n\n- Verify whether an email address is deliverable, disposable or suspicious (domain database + AI matching).\n- Validate phone numbers and flag fraud or invalid formats.\n- Score IP addresses for VPN/proxy/suspicious origin.\n- Validate other identifiers: cryptocurrency wallets, domains/URLs, credit cards, user agents and IBANs.\n- Password-strength validation via a public endpoint.\n\nThe API has a public branch (no token required) and a private branch that needs an API key issued from a Dymo account. Note: this is the TPEOficial \"Dymo\" data-validation API and is unrelated to the Dymo label-printer products from Newell Brands.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "security": "Data-validation and fraud-detection operations covering email, phone, IP, crypto wallet, domain/URL, credit card, user agent, IBAN and password strength."
        },
